WEBVTT

s1.1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.206
The Symphony plugin brings Symphony into Tern.

s1.2
00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:08.756
It shows what the agents do, opens live chats, and covers the merger and team administration.

s1.3
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:14.683
Run Symphony: Sign in, then enter your team's address and the API token an admin created for you.

s1.4
00:00:14.683 --> 00:00:19.167
The token is masked. The symphony CLI stores it in the system keychain.

s1.5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:24.755
Tern never stores it. The plugin asks the CLI for the token and keeps it in memory only.

s1.6
00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:31.310
Install in Tern adds the live chat agent and the MCP server for your omp. The plugin is already there.

s1.7
00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.145
When you are not signed in, the panel and the status line show the next step.

s1.8
00:00:35.145 --> 00:00:39.520
If Symphony goes down, the panel keeps the last data and shows Offline.

s2.1
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.057
Control Alt S opens the Dashboard.

s2.2
00:00:42.057 --> 00:00:46.199
It shows the day's numbers, and the providers' rate limits of the last hour.

s2.3
00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:52.106
Below, six tiles cover the last 30 days, up to the tickets blocked on a person, with the cost per day.

s2.4
00:00:52.106 --> 00:00:56.591
Sessions that need input come first, with the agent's question and its options.

s2.5
00:00:56.591 --> 00:00:59.865
Press A to answer. Pick an option, or write your own answer.

s2.6
00:00:59.865 --> 00:01:04.928
Press M to send a message. If the agent is running, the message joins the current turn.

s2.7
00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:07.391
Press I to interrupt, after a confirmation.

s2.8
00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:11.392
Press T to take over. Symphony takeover then runs in a new tab.

s2.9
00:01:11.392 --> 00:01:15.344
The status line shows how many agents run, and how many need input.

s2.10
00:01:15.344 --> 00:01:19.559
It is highlighted when an agent waits for you, and says paused or offline.

s3.1
00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:25.257
Sessions lists every session. The bracket keys filter Active, Needs input, Ended or All.

s3.2
00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:29.231
Control Alt A picks a session and opens its live chat in a new tab.

s3.3
00:01:29.231 --> 00:01:34.179
It is a native Tern chat through symphony acp, with the history and the live events.

s3.4
00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:41.914
Its first line names the pod, the repository and the branch. Nothing runs on this machine, and the tab opens in an empty folder.

s3.5
00:01:41.914 --> 00:01:44.934
While the agent runs, your message steers the current turn.

s3.6
00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:49.463
When it is idle, the message is a follow-up. When it asks, the message is the answer.

s3.7
00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:51.937
To stop the agent, type slash interrupt.

s3.8
00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:57.499
Take over holds the ticket, downloads the conversation and the branch, and opens omp on your machine.

s3.9
00:01:57.499 --> 00:01:59.424
Return it with symphony release.

s4.1
00:01:59.774 --> 00:02:05.540
Tickets shows each ticket's state in Symphony and on the board, the attempt, the cost and the pull request.

s4.2
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.718
Symphony does not dispatch a ticket that a person holds.

s4.3
00:02:08.718 --> 00:02:12.675
Return to Symphony releases it, and the agents can work on it again.

s5.1
00:02:13.025 --> 00:02:19.218
One merger serves every repository with a merger policy. Control Alt M opens the Merger view.

s5.2
00:02:19.218 --> 00:02:24.629
Mergers lists each repository: whether it runs, who holds its train lease, and its current batch.

s5.3
00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:29.456
Takes says which pull requests it reviews: every one, or only those with its labels.

s5.4
00:02:29.456 --> 00:02:34.748
A parked review shows the pull request's title, and whether it waits for CI or for an approval.

s5.5
00:02:34.748 --> 00:02:40.030
Each table has a Repository column, so pull requests of two repositories never mix.

s5.6
00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:45.431
On the selected pull request, B bypasses the review. It asks for a reason for the audit log.

s5.7
00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.214
Q requeues the pull request, and L releases it.

s5.8
00:02:48.214 --> 00:02:51.756
Each action carries the repository of that pull request.

s6.1
00:02:52.106 --> 00:02:54.019
Five more views, for every role.

s6.2
00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:59.046
Repositories lists every repository Symphony reaches, with the values it detected.

s6.3
00:02:59.046 --> 00:03:03.461
An admin presses E to configure its runtime, base branch and components.

s6.4
00:03:03.461 --> 00:03:06.827
Infrastructure shows the services and the cluster resources.

s6.5
00:03:06.827 --> 00:03:10.234
Telemetry shows usage by model, by month and by session.

s6.6
00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:14.867
Its History charts ten views of the daily rollups. The bracket keys pick the period.

s6.7
00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:18.230
Learnings shows the retrospectives and learning pull requests.

s6.8
00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.216
Audit lists what people and agents asked Symphony to do.

s6.9
00:03:21.216 --> 00:03:24.846
When a source is stale or unavailable, the view says which one.

s7.1
00:03:25.196 --> 00:03:27.605
The Admin view needs an admin token.

s7.2
00:03:27.605 --> 00:03:30.792
Models sets the model and the thinking level of each role.

s7.3
00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:34.563
Enter picks a model from the pinned omp catalog, then the thinking level.

s7.4
00:03:34.563 --> 00:03:38.142
The change stays marked until you publish it with P and a reason.

s7.5
00:03:38.142 --> 00:03:40.919
If someone else published first, nothing is overwritten.

s7.6
00:03:40.919 --> 00:03:44.537
The rollout shows which consumers already applied the new generation.

s7.7
00:03:44.537 --> 00:03:47.783
Providers stores the API keys that the models use.

s7.8
00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:54.286
C sets or replaces a key in a hidden field. The key is write-only: it never comes back through the API.

s7.9
00:03:54.286 --> 00:03:57.956
It applies on each agent's next attempt, without a restart.

s8.1
00:03:58.306 --> 00:04:03.456
Tokens creates team API tokens, each with a name, a role and an expiry.

s8.2
00:04:03.456 --> 00:04:07.414
A viewer watches, an operator also acts, and an admin administers.

s8.3
00:04:07.414 --> 00:04:11.246
A new token appears only once. After I saved it, it is gone.

s8.4
00:04:11.246 --> 00:04:14.259
X revokes a token at once, after a confirmation.

s8.5
00:04:14.259 --> 00:04:19.916
MCP servers give agents more tools. Each role gets only the servers enabled for it.

s8.6
00:04:19.916 --> 00:04:22.148
Enter tests a server and lists its tools.

s8.7
00:04:22.148 --> 00:04:27.299
Secret headers are write-only. The gateway adds them, so no secret reaches an agent.

s8.8
00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:33.013
Skills lists the central skill sources: each one's repository, scope, commit and number of skills.

s8.9
00:04:33.013 --> 00:04:38.488
Team omp shows the workers' omp defaults. S applies them to your omp, in a separate profile.

s9.1
00:04:38.838 --> 00:04:40.979
The palette has a command for each view.

s9.2
00:04:40.979 --> 00:04:47.031
Control Alt S opens the Dashboard, Control Alt M the Merger, and Control Alt A a live chat.

s9.3
00:04:47.031 --> 00:04:52.503
In the panel, tab switches views, the arrows or J and K select, and enter opens the chat.

s9.4
00:04:52.503 --> 00:04:56.149
R refreshes, and Control P pauses or resumes the daemon.

s9.5
00:04:56.149 --> 00:04:58.982
Each footer shows only the keys that your role can use.

s9.6
00:04:58.982 --> 00:05:03.583
A confirmation opens above the footer. Enter confirms, and escape cancels.

s9.7
00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:08.822
Pause, bypass and publish need a reason of at least eight characters, for the audit log.
